+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`TaskList.add` already validates title, priority and tags and rejects duplicate titles, returning a `Result`. The domain never throws and reads no clock; the list supplies ids and times.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Parse lines and add them through `list.add`, so validation and ids stay in one place.
+- Report each rejected line with its 1-based number and a readable reason.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Quoting or escaping `;` in titles, other separators, or rolling back on rejection.
+- Changing the `TaskList` interface.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- New `src/domain/import.ts` with `importTasks(list, text)`, re-exported from `src/index.ts` with its result types. It is pure over the list given; it never throws.
+- Each line is split on `;`; more than three parts is rejected. Priority is passed to `list.add` as text, and an invalid value is reported using `validatePriority`'s message (checked before `add`, since `add` takes a typed `Priority`).
+- The reason is the `error.message` of the failed result, so messages stay consistent with `add`.
+- Duplicates (in the list or earlier in the text) come from `add`'s own `duplicate` failure.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Titles containing `;` cannot be imported; they are rejected as having too many parts.
