+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Teams are moving to Tidy Tasks from spreadsheets and need to load many tasks at once instead of adding them one by one.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `importTasks(list, text)`: reads one task per line as `title;priority;tags`, adds every valid line to the list, and reports how many were added and which lines were rejected and why.
+- Blank lines are skipped; an empty priority means `normal`; tags are separated by spaces.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-import`: bulk import of tasks from text, one per line.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- Rules touched: TSDoc on every exported function (the new function has one); errors in the domain are never thrown (the parser returns rejections as data and never throws); no clock or randomness (time and ids come from the list); no new dependency.
+- Public API: `src/index.ts` changes: it exports `importTasks` and the type `ImportResult` (and `ImportRejection`).
+- New code in `src/domain/import.ts`; tests in `test/import.test.ts`. `TaskList` is unchanged.
