+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+Lets people load many tasks into the list at once from text, such as lines copied from a spreadsheet, and tells them which lines could not be added.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Import tasks from text
+`importTasks(list, text)` SHALL read `text` one line per task, in the form `title;priority;tags`, add every valid line to `list` and return `{ imported, rejected }`. `imported` SHALL be the number of tasks added. Lines SHALL be split on `\n` or `\r\n`. The title SHALL be trimmed. The priority SHALL be trimmed; if empty or absent, the task is `normal`. Tags SHALL be separated by spaces (any run of whitespace), and the tags part MAY be empty or absent. Lines that are empty or only whitespace SHALL be skipped and are neither imported nor rejected.
+
+#### Scenario: Full line
+- **WHEN** the text is `Renew the insurance;high;admin money`
+- **THEN** a task "Renew the insurance" with priority `high` and tags `admin`, `money` is added, and the result is `{ imported: 1, rejected: [] }`
+
+#### Scenario: Empty priority and no tags
+- **WHEN** the text is `Buy milk;;` or `Buy milk`
+- **THEN** a `normal` task "Buy milk" with no tags is added
+
+#### Scenario: Blank lines skipped
+- **WHEN** the text has blank lines between tasks, or is empty
+- **THEN** only the task lines are imported and nothing is rejected
+
+### Requirement: Rejected lines are reported
+Every non-blank line that cannot be added SHALL be listed in `rejected` as `{ line, reason }`, in text order. `line` SHALL be the line's number in `text`, counting from 1 and counting blank lines. `reason` SHALL be a message for the person using the app saying what is wrong. A rejected line SHALL NOT stop the other lines from being imported. A line is rejected when its title is empty or too long (code `invalid-input` of `add`), its priority is not `low`, `normal` or `high`, a tag is invalid, it has more than three `;`-separated parts, or its title is already in the list or earlier in the text (`duplicate`).
+
+#### Scenario: Invalid priority
+- **WHEN** a line is `Pay rent;urgent;money`
+- **THEN** it is rejected with a reason naming the priority, and the list is unchanged by it
+
+#### Scenario: Empty title
+- **WHEN** a line is `;high;admin`
+- **THEN** it is rejected with a reason saying the title is empty
+
+#### Scenario: Too many parts
+- **WHEN** a line is `Call; then email;high;admin`
+- **THEN** it is rejected with a reason saying the line has too many parts
+
+#### Scenario: Duplicate title
+- **WHEN** a line's title is already in the list, or appeared on an earlier line
+- **THEN** that line is rejected with a reason saying the task already exists
+
+#### Scenario: Line numbers
+- **WHEN** the text is `Good task`, a blank line, then `Bad;nope`
+- **THEN** the result is `imported: 1` and `rejected` holds one entry with `line: 3`
+
+#### Scenario: Valid lines survive bad ones
+- **WHEN** some lines are rejected
+- **THEN** every other valid line is still added to the list
